122057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122057","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122057.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122057.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-04T16:52:30Z"},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nDoing `find_keycode_from_string(\"Windows\")` on a non-Windows platform returns `KEY_NONE`. That's rather unexpected...\r\n\r\nI recently discovered my addon does not work properly on Linux, because I was using Windows keycode. And what's worse, making `get_keycode_string()` work properly on all platforms is not trivial and requires knowledge about platform-specific keycode strings, which weren't documented.\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes that by making all platforms recognize all strings. Calling `get_keycode_string(\"Windows\")` will now return `KEY_META` on all platforms.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nUnfortunately I wasn't able to get rid of  `defined()` checks, leading to quite a bit duplicate code. This is to ensure that `get_keycode_string()` works correctly.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","sub